#: src/pages/CardDetailPage.tsx
msgid "出片时一段里只有「第一张人物卡」能带形象参考图：它最多取 {MAX_CHAR_REFS} 张（优先{face} + {body}）；同一段里的其余人物卡一张都不带，只按文字设定参与——一张图里画多个角色会被方舟整条拒掉。所以上面的「出片用」是按\"这张卡就是那第一张人物卡\"标的：它排在别的人物卡后面时，标着出片用的那几张同样进不了模型（生成步骤里会点名说明）。（两条不画设定帧的路是例外——白模模板挂卡、简约模式的参考图直出：每张人物卡都各带自己的形象图。）{detail}这一格铸卡不会自动出图（只能自己传），三张挂满时它也排在最后，出片轮不到它。"
msgstr "When making videos, only the “first character card” in a segment can bring reference images: it takes at most {MAX_CHAR_REFS, plural, one {# image} other {# images}} ({face} + {body} first). Other character cards in the same segment bring none and only take part through their text details — one image with several characters gets rejected outright by Ark. So “Used in video” above assumes this card is that first character card: if it comes after other character cards, the images marked Used in video won't reach the model either (the generation steps will say so). (The two paths that don't draw setup frames are exceptions — attaching cards to a blockout template, and direct reference-image output in Simple mode: every character card brings its own images.) The {detail} slot isn't generated automatically when minting (you can only upload it yourself), and when all three are filled it comes last, so it never gets used in videos."

#. placeholder {0}: CARD_INFO_LABELS[card.type]
#: src/pages/CardDetailPage.tsx
msgid "出片时提示词里代表这张卡的固定一句（逐段复用同一措辞，形象更稳）。长设定进画面靠上面的参考图与{0}，不直接塞进视频提示词。"
msgstr "The fixed line that stands for this card in video prompts (the same wording is reused in every segment, which keeps the look steadier). Longer details reach the picture through the reference images above and the {0}; they aren't stuffed into the video prompt."

#: src/pages/CardDetailPage.tsx
msgid "出片时这类卡先保证第 1 张（{first}）喂给 AI；同一段里参考图总共最多 {MAX_REF_IMAGES} 张，预算还有余才轮得到第 2 张 —— 也就是同段挂的卡越少，它越可能真的进模型。预算不够时「先被丢的就是各卡的第 2 张」，卡再多下去整张卡都会带不上（两种情况生成步骤里都会逐张点名）。（白模挂卡与简约参考图直出那两条路更宽：参考图直接进视频模型，上限按所选档位的协议走。）"
msgstr "When making videos, this kind of card always gets its first image ({first}) fed to the AI. A segment takes at most {MAX_REF_IMAGES, plural, one {# reference image} other {# reference images}} in total, and the second image only gets in if there's budget left — so the fewer cards in the segment, the more likely it actually reaches the model. When the budget runs short, “each card's second image is dropped first”, and with even more cards whole cards get left out (the generation steps name each one in both cases). (Attaching cards to a blockout template and direct reference-image output in Simple mode are more generous: reference images go straight into the video model, up to the limit of the chosen tier.)"

